{%- comment -%}
  What Is ErsatzReality — preview theme only.
  Answers the four things a first-time visitor has no way to learn today:
  what this is, how the pieces connect, why evidence is the point, and what
  they can actually do here.
{%- endcomment -%}

<style>
  .ea{--ink:#0d0e10;--ink2:#16181c;--paper:#f4f1ea;--dim:#cfc9bc;--mute:#9a948a;
      --amber:#d9a441;--line:rgba(244,241,234,.14);
      --serif:"Iowan Old Style","Palatino Linotype",Palatino,Georgia,serif;
      background:var(--ink);color:var(--paper);display:block}
  .ea *{box-sizing:border-box;min-width:0}
  .ea-w{max-width:780px;margin:0 auto;padding:0 16px}
  .ea-hero{padding:60px 0 42px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}
  .ea-kick{font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.26em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--amber);margin:0 0 16px}
  .ea h1{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(28px,5.2vw,46px);line-height:1.14;margin:0 0 16px}
  .ea h2{font-family:var(--serif);font-weight:500;font-size:clamp(19px,3vw,26px);margin:44px 0 12px}
  .ea p{font-size:16.5px;line-height:1.62;color:var(--dim);margin:0 0 16px}
  .ea .lead{font-size:clamp(17px,2.2vw,19.5px);color:var(--paper)}
  .ea-sec{padding:4px 0 48px}
  .ea-steps{list-style:none;margin:18px 0 0;padding:0;display:grid;gap:10px}
  .ea-steps li{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;padding:15px 16px;background:var(--ink2)}
  .ea-steps b{color:var(--amber);font-size:11px;letter-spacing:.16em;text-transform:uppercase;display:block;margin-bottom:5px}
  .ea-steps span{font-size:14.5px;color:var(--dim);line-height:1.5}
  .ea-reg{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(auto-fit,minmax(150px,1fr));gap:10px;margin:18px 0 0}
  .ea-reg div{border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:3px;padding:14px;background:var(--ink2)}
  .ea-reg h3{margin:0 0 6px;font-size:12px;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase;color:var(--amber);font-weight:700}
  .ea-reg p{margin:0;font-size:13.5px;color:var(--mute);line-height:1.5}
  .ea-note{border-left:2px solid var(--amber);padding:2px 0 2px 15px;color:var(--dim);font-size:15px;margin:26px 0 0}
</style>

<div class="ea">
  <section class="ea-hero"><div class="ea-w">
    <p class="ea-kick">What is ErsatzReality</p>
    <h1>{{ section.settings.headline | escape }}</h1>
    <p class="lead">{{ section.settings.lead | escape }}</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="ea-sec"><div class="ea-w">
    <h2>The rule everything here follows</h2>
    <p>Most writing mixes what is known, what is believed and what is hoped, then prints the mixture
      in one typeface. ErsatzReality refuses to. Every product keeps four registers apart, and says
      which one it is speaking in.</p>
    <div class="ea-reg">
      <div><h3>Documented</h3><p>There is a source, and we name it.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Tradition</h3><p>People have long said so. That is a fact about people, not about the thing.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Science</h3><p>What testing currently supports, including where it disagrees.</p></div>
      <div><h3>Unknown</h3><p>Nobody has established this. It stays marked unknown rather than quietly filled in.</p></div>
    </div>
    <p class="ea-note">This is why a story here ends on a question instead of a moral, and why a
      notebook about a vehicle can honestly say there is no car at the end of it.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="ea-sec"><div class="ea-w">
    <h2>How the pieces connect</h2>
    <p>A world, a story, a question, a tool and a product are not five separate businesses here.
      They are five points on one chain, and each one is made from the one before it.</p>
    <ol class="ea-steps">
      <li><b>The world</b><span>EdereAriah has trades, weather, people and arguments that are not settled. Nothing in it is decoration.</span></li>
      <li><b>A story</b><span>Something happens to someone in that world. It is written down as an edition you can read tonight.</span></li>
      <li><b>A question</b><span>The story leaves a question standing. It goes on the record with what is documented, believed and unknown about it.</span></li>
      <li><b>A tool</b><span>The question turns into something you can use — a deck, a workbook, a hunt — that works on your own life, not only ours.</span></li>
      <li><b>A product</b><span>The tool becomes a file you keep. Downloading it again next year costs nothing and does not expire.</span></li>
    </ol>
  </div></section>

  <section class="ea-sec"><div class="ea-w">
    <h2>Why evidence is the point, not the decoration</h2>
    <p>It would be faster to write a confident answer. It would also be worth less. A confident answer
      you cannot check is indistinguishable from a made-up one, and a world built out of confident
      answers collapses the moment somebody looks closely.</p>
    <p>So the working is shown. When the record is contested, the file reports the contest rather than
      picking the pleasing version. When something is genuinely unknown, it is written down precisely
      enough that somebody could go and find out.</p>
  </div></section>

  <section class="ea-sec"><div class="ea-w">
    <h2>What you can do here</h2>
    <ol class="ea-steps">
      <li><b>Read something tonight</b><span>Short finished editions. They arrive in your library and stay yours.</span></li>
      <li><b>Follow a question</b><span>Take a question with no settled answer and see the evidence on either side of it.</span></li>
      <li><b>Learn how it works</b><span>The working methods, not the theory. You come out with something built.</span></li>
      <li><b>Walk around the world</b><span>Free. No purchase. The world is the point; the shop is downstream of it.</span></li>
      <li><b>Keep it</b><span>Everything is a file. Nothing ships, nothing expires, and re-downloading costs nothing.</span></li>
    </ol>
    <p class="ea-note">{{ section.settings.closing | escape }}</p>
  </div></section>
</div>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "ER about",
  "tag": "section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "headline", "label": "Headline", "default": "A world that shows its working." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "lead", "label": "Lead", "default": "ErsatzReality is a made world, built in public, where every object we sell is the end of an investigation rather than the start of a pitch." },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "closing", "label": "Closing note", "default": "If you only do one thing: read the cheapest story on the shelf. It is short, it is finished, and it will tell you more about what this place is than any page about us can." }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "ER about" }]
}
{% endschema %}
